@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Advanced Docker Topics";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="text-center lead">
        Beyond the basics, Docker supports advanced use cases such as GUI applications, multi-architecture builds, GPU acceleration, and system-level debugging.
        Mastering these topics enhances your ability to use Docker in complex, real-world environments.
    </p>
    <hr />

    <!-- Section: Running GUI Applications in Docker -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Running GUI Applications in Docker</h2>
        <p>Linux GUI apps can be run in containers using X11 forwarding:</p>
        <div class="code-snippet bg-light p-3 rounded position-relative">
            <pre class="mb-0"><code>docker run -e DISPLAY=$DISPLAY \
    -v /tmp/.X11-unix:/tmp/.X11-unix \
    gui-app-image</code></pre>
            <button class="btn btn-outline-secondary copy-btn position-absolute top-0 end-0 m-2">Copy</button>
        </div>
        <p>For Windows or macOS, tools like VNC or XQuartz are used to view GUI apps from containers.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Section: Debugging Containers -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Debugging Containers</h3>
        <p>Use interactive shell access to inspect containers:</p>
        <div class="code-snippet bg-light p-3 rounded position-relative">
            <pre class="mb-0"><code>docker exec -it container_name /bin/bash</code></pre>
            <button class="btn btn-outline-secondary copy-btn position-absolute top-0 end-0 m-2">Copy</button>
        </div>
        <p>Use logging tools and inspect commands to trace issues:</p>
        <div class="code-snippet bg-light p-3 rounded position-relative">
            <pre class="mb-0"><code>docker logs container_name
docker inspect container_name</code></pre>
            <button class="btn btn-outline-secondary copy-btn position-absolute top-0 end-0 m-2">Copy</button>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Section: Multi-Arch Builds -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Multi-Arch Builds (ARM & x86)</h3>
        <p>Use Docker Buildx to build for multiple architectures:</p>
        <div class="code-snippet bg-light p-3 rounded position-relative">
            <pre class="mb-0"><code>docker buildx create --use
docker buildx build --platform linux/amd64,linux/arm64 -t myapp:multiarch --push .</code></pre>
            <button class="btn btn-outline-secondary copy-btn position-absolute top-0 end-0 m-2">Copy</button>
        </div>
        <p>This allows you to support both desktop and ARM devices like Raspberry Pi.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Section: Using Docker with GPU -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Using Docker with GPU (for AI/ML)</h3>
        <p>Enable NVIDIA GPU support with Docker using the <code>nvidia-container-toolkit</code>:</p>
        <div class="code-snippet bg-light p-3 rounded position-relative">
            <pre class="mb-0"><code>docker run --gpus all nvidia/cuda:11.8.0-base nvidia-smi</code></pre>
            <button class="btn btn-outline-secondary copy-btn position-absolute top-0 end-0 m-2">Copy</button>
        </div>
        <p>Great for machine learning, deep learning, or GPU-intensive applications.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Section: Windows vs Linux Containers -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Windows Containers vs. Linux Containers</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Windows containers can only run on Windows hosts (or Windows Server Core base images)</li>
            <li>Linux containers are portable across environments and more widely supported</li>
            <li>Use Docker Desktop to switch between Linux and Windows container modes</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Summary -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <p>
            These advanced features unlock Docker’s full potential for enterprise systems, development pipelines,
            and high-performance computing. Explore these capabilities to scale your infrastructure intelligently.
        </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Navigation Buttons -->
    <div class="d-flex justify-content-between mt-4">
        <a href="@Url.Action("CICDWithDocker", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">
            &larr; Previous: CI/CD with Docker
        </a>
        <a href="@Url.Action("DockerMigration", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">
            Next: Docker Container Migration &rarr;
        </a>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- Copy Script -->
<script>
    document.querySelectorAll('.copy-btn').forEach(btn => {
        btn.addEventListener('click', function () {
            const codeText = this.parentElement.querySelector('code')?.innerText;
            if (codeText) {
                navigator.clipboard.writeText(codeText).then(() => {
                    alert('Code copied to clipboard!');
                });
            }
        });
    });
</script>
